### Example 1 — Mobile app

**Project description:** A fintech startup needs a mobile app (iOS and Android) for
peer-to-peer money transfers between friends. Users sign up with phone number
verification, link a bank card, and send/request money with a note attached. Push
notifications confirm each transfer. A transaction history screen shows the last 90
days of activity.

**Estimation:**

## Project summary
Cross-platform mobile app for peer-to-peer transfers, including onboarding,
card linking, transfer flows, and push notifications.

## Phases
| Phase | Hours | Cost (EUR) |
|-------|------:|------------|
| Onboarding and phone verification | 24 | 1,500 |
| Card linking (Stripe Issuing) | 20 | 1,250 |
| Send/request money flow | 32 | 2,000 |
| Push notifications | 12 | 750 |
| Transaction history | 16 | 1,000 |
| Testing and QA | 20 | 1,250 |

## Totals
- Total hours: 124
- Total cost: 7,750 EUR
- Recommended team: 1 senior mobile developer, 1 backend developer
- Estimated duration: 6 weeks

## Risks and assumptions
- Assumes a single banking provider integration (no multi-bank support in this phase)
- Push notification delivery depends on third-party services (APNs/FCM)
- Regulatory/KYC requirements are out of scope for this estimation

